sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Shared Du and Dv/Du = 10, species-specific basal activator a. Onset wavelength is 3.101 µm for D. virilis (a = 0.10), 2.924 µm for predecessor D. teissieri (a = 0.058, still unstable), and no selected wavenumber for successor D. willistoni (a = 0.360, discriminant negative). All three are Holocene (0 Ma). Linearized dispersion Pearson r = 0.998 against continuum σ(k) (RMSE 0.032). Equal-diffusion ablation quenches activator std from 0.043 to 0. Saturated midline spacing is 3.625 µm, not the onset value. The Hanson 2019 habitus has a Nyquist length of 7.76 µm and does not resolve 3.1 µm. Overall 86.3/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_virilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 564225 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e (sha256 f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e), spec_fingerprint 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8; artifact_sha256: f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber selection from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the steady state u0 = a + b, v0 = b/(a+b)^2. | Gompel et al. 2005: abdominal pigment differences among Drosophila species are cis-regulatory, including posterior bands in the melanogaster subgroup. | Hanson 2019 CC BY-SA 4.0 lateral habitus of Drosophila virilis (Wikimedia File:Dvir 1-2.jpg).; reconstructed_in_script: Du solved so virilis onset λ_c = 3.101 µm at Dv/Du = 10 and b = 0.90. | Teissieri a = 0.058 and willistoni a = 0.360 as the chronoseries step at fixed age and fixed diffusivities. | Tergite mode counts from project atlas adult lengths divided by seven. | Adult GIF endpoint is the habitus photograph modulated by the normalized PDE field.; transfer_boundary: The 3.101 µm target is the slot scale. It is not a published ocellus measurement for D. virilis. | Atlas body lengths are used only to turn a wavelength into a mode count.; does_not_claim: That the habitus photograph resolves a 3.1 µm pigment wavelength (measured Nyquist is 7.76 µm). | That willistoni lost a Turing pattern through geological time (successor is extant, 0 Ma). | That chorion-filament number enters the wavenumber law. | That the PDE generated the wing veins or the body outline.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=5.0]: Fixed 48 by 32 µm patch. No growing ocellar disc, so mode insertion with domain length is not demonstrated.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: One lateral habitus. Pixel scale cannot confirm the 3.101 µm mode.",
            "remediation needed: R1. The PDE lives on a fixed 48 by 32 µm patch. Add a domain-length series and show that the number of activator peaks increases with patch length (mode count), which this pass does not measure.",
            "remediation needed: R2. The Hanson habitus Nyquist length is 7.76 µm. Keep that as an explicit negative result: the photograph is not evidence for the 3.101 µm wavelength.",
            "remediation needed: R3. Basal activator levels are reconstructed from pigmentation class. They are not a fit to a measured virilis concentration series.",
            "remediation needed: R4. Scores are from one assessor." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.863"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

